Read the full plan first: C:\Users\jande\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\D--oh-my-posh\6c0a282a-886f-458d-a426-93d95104b4a6\scratchpad\phase2a-plan.md — then implement ONLY the section titled "Task B — catalog component and page". Also read "Data contract — PINNED": that is the exact shape you consume, and you may not change it.

You own exactly three files and must touch nothing else:
- `website/src/components/SegmentCatalog/index.js` (new)
- `website/src/components/SegmentCatalog/styles.module.css` (new)
- `website/src/pages/segments.js` (new)

Explicitly NOT yours: `website/docusaurus.config.js`, `website/plugins/**`, `website/docs/**`, `website/src/pages/index.js`, `website/src/pages/styles.module.css`.

A parallel task is building the plugin that supplies your data. Build against the pinned contract; do not wait for it. If `usePluginData` returns undefined during your local testing, that is the plugin not being registered yet — the coordinator wires it up.

The four things most likely to go wrong, all covered in detail in the plan:

1. **Hydration.** Docusaurus SSR renders `<StaticRouter location={pathname}>` — pathname only, NO query string. If you initialise filter state from `useLocation().search` during the first client render, `/segments?group=cli` produces 39 cards against the server's 117 and React 19 discards the whole server tree. Avoiding `window`/`document` does NOT fix this; `useLocation()` is the leak. Use `useIsBrowser()` from `@docusaurus/useIsBrowser`, which is false on the server and on the first client render. The server HTML must contain all 117 cards unfiltered — that is the SEO and Algolia requirement.

2. **Card fill must be theme-split.** `--ifm-background-surface-color` is `#fff` in light mode, identical to the page canvas, so a card using it has a border and no fill. `--ifm-color-emphasis-100` is invisible in dark. Use the split given in the plan.

3. **Auth tag contrast.** Do NOT use `--ifm-color-warning-darkest` — 3.44:1 on white, below the AA bar. Use `--ifm-color-warning-contrast-foreground` / `--ifm-color-warning-contrast-background`.

4. **Do not bind ⌘K or Ctrl-K.** Algolia DocSearch owns that chord sitewide. No global keyboard shortcut at all.

Also: namespace facet React keys as `${facet}:${id}` — `groups` and `authTiers` both contain an id of `cli`.

Design reference — this is retoned from an approved mockup that was drawn in a fixed dark palette. Use Infima CSS variables throughout so it works in both themes; do not lift the mockup's hardcoded colours:

```
.cat     { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 13.5rem 1fr; }
.facets  { border-right: 1px solid RULE; padding: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
.grp     { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
.lbl     { font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: MUTED; }
label    { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; font-size: 0.78rem; }
.ct      { margin-left: auto; font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.68rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.grid    { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px, 1fr)); gap: 0.7rem; }
.item    { border: 1px solid RULE; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
.nm      { font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.82rem; }
.ds      { font-size: 0.73rem; color: MUTED; line-height: 1.45; }
.tag     { font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; padding: 0.08rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 3px; border: 1px solid RULE; }
@media (max-width: 700px) { .cat { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .facets { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid RULE; } }
```

Repo conventions — read `website/src/components/Config.js` and `website/src/components/Auth.js` first: plain function declarations (not arrow consts), `import React from 'react'`, `export default X;` at the bottom, CSS modules, `classnames` for conditional classes (already a dependency). React 19.

Use real `<input type="checkbox">` elements, visually restyled. The mockup faked them with spans only because it was static artwork. Keep the page keyboard-accessible and the facet groups in `<fieldset>`/`<legend>`.

Verify before reporting: `npm run build` from `website/` (it will fail on the missing plugin until the coordinator wires it — if so, say exactly that and confirm your files have no other errors). Report: files created, how you handled hydration, and anything in the plan that turned out to be wrong.

