Also: namespace facet React keys as `${facet}:${id}` — `groups` and `authTiers` both contain an id of `cli`.

Design reference — this is retoned from an approved mockup that was drawn in a fixed dark palette. Use Infima CSS variables throughout so it works in both themes; do not lift the mockup's hardcoded colours:

```
.cat     { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 13.5rem 1fr; }
.facets  { border-right: 1px solid RULE; padding: 1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
.grp     { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
.lbl     { font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; color: MUTED; }
label    { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; font-size: 0.78rem; }
.ct      { margin-left: auto; font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.68rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
.grid    { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px, 1fr)); gap: 0.7rem; }
.item    { border: 1px solid RULE; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
.nm      { font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.82rem; }
.ds      { font-size: 0.73rem; color: MUTED; line-height: 1.45; }
.tag     { font-family: MONO; font-size: 0.6rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; padding: 0.08rem 0.35rem; border-radius: 3px; border: 1px solid RULE; }
@media (max-width: 700px) { .cat { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .facets { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid RULE; } }
```

Repo conventions — read `website/src/components/Config.js` and `website/src/components/Auth.js` first: plain function declarations (not arrow consts), `import React from 'react'`, `export default X;` at the bottom, CSS modules, `classnames` for conditional classes (already a dependency). React 19.

Use real `<input type="checkbox">` elements, visually restyled. The mockup faked them with spans only because it was static artwork. Keep the page keyboard-accessible and the facet groups in `<fieldset>`/`<legend>`.

Verify before reporting: `npm run build` from `website/` (it will fail on the missing plugin until the coordinator wires it — if so, say exactly that and confirm your files have no other errors). Report: files created, how you handled hydration, and anything in the plan that turned out to be wrong.

