/* VictorMono.ttf is the Mono patched Nerd Font variant (VictorMono NFM), not
   the plain one. Both patch the same 11,658 codepoints at the same advance,
   so nothing about the grid changes - but the plain variant leaves an icon's
   ink at its natural width while still advancing one cell, and Nerd Font
   icons are far wider than a cell: U+F07B (folder) inks 1.693 cells, U+F120
   (terminal) 1.903. That ink runs over whatever follows the icon, which in
   the theme gallery is the space each segment template writes after it. The
   Mono variant scales every icon to exactly one cell. Keep this variant when
   versioning the font up. */
@font-face {
  font-family: "Victor Mono";
  src: url('/fonts/VictorMono.ttf') format("truetype");
  font-display: swap;
}

